WEBVTT

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:26.359
Destroy the Council President?

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:27.944
Yeah.

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:31.197
I… I don't understand what you mean.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:34.034
Why would you wanna hurt her
if you're on the Council?

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:40.248
-Because of this.
-[Mary gasping]

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:41.750
MITTENS

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.835
Don't you think this is a little much?

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.464
They treat you like an animal
just for losing a game.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.506
It's wrong.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.843
The Student Council President
created this system.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:53.511
I want to dismantle it.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:01:00.268
If you're willing to help me out,
then I'll give you this million back.

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:03.521
I know we can do it, Mary.

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.315
I just need your help.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:11.738
I'm sorry.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.283
All of this is my fault.
He messed everything up.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:16.284
Huh?

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.747
No. You don't need to say sorry.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.917
And don't blame yourself for a scenario
that I didn't prepare myself for.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.587
Mary, no! Please don't blame yourself
when you weren't the one playing.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.297
Now, now! Calm down.

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:32.550
Isn't placing blame
just a waste of energy?

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.969
We should be focusing
on how to bring money into the den--

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:36.304
Don't be stupid!

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:39.265
How are we gonna do that without a buy-in?

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:43.561
[both groaning]

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:48.399
Heading home.

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.659
[indistinct chatter]

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:02.080
<i>It's no use.</i>
<i>I don't have the headspace for this.</i>

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:04.916
Are you kidding me?

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.712
It's that time of year.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.340
Oh crap.
Do I have anything saved up?

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:14.467
STUDENT COUNCIL DONATION DEADLINE NOTICE

00:02:16.052 --> 00:02:19.097
Hey, uh… Do you know what this is?

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.640
What? You can't read?

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:22.976
It's announcing the due date
for Student Council donations.

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:25.145
Oh. Right.

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:26.729
So…

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.482
If you don't pay up,
you'll be a house pet.

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:30.984
So, you'd better be careful.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:34.195
<i>This is bad.</i>
<i>I don't have any cash right now.</i>

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:37.240
<i>I won't be able to help Tsuzura at all</i>
<i>if I'm the one that ends up…</i>

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.491
MITTENS

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:40.618
<i>And if I'm a house pet too,</i>

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:45.582
<i>then neither of us would have any hope</i>
<i>of becoming human until we graduate.</i>

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:30.960
TWIN

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.013
[knocking on door]

00:03:42.096 --> 00:03:42.972
Come in.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.102
I had a feeling you'd show up
right about now.

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:51.189
What are you two doing in here?

00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:52.106
Well, uh…

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.858
I invited them here.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.109
Huh?

00:03:55.193 --> 00:03:56.319
You came all this way,

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:59.822
so I assume what I said
was a little intriguing to you.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:03.243
I haven't decided
if I want to accept your offer.

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:04.702
That's totally fine.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.079
For a long time,

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:08.748
the power of the Student Council
has gone completely unchecked.

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:11.376
No one has any ability to confront them.

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:14.254
And it's all because
of this tiered system they made.

00:04:14.337 --> 00:04:17.006
The threat of becoming
a house pet is enough

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.510
for students to lose any motivation
to rise against the Student Council.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.054
They get comfortable
with the way things are,

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:26.015
which only encourages them
to maintain the status quo.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.601
Gotta admit
they really thought it through.

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:32.105
People get to be petty,
and the Student Council stays comfy.

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:33.898
So, what do we do about it?

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:36.401
I say we destroy the system.

00:04:43.491 --> 00:04:44.659
What the hell?

00:04:44.742 --> 00:04:45.660
FIDO

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:46.661
MITTENS

00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:47.662
FIDO

00:04:49.205 --> 00:04:50.540
Is everyone in here a--

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.917
Yes. They're all house pets.

00:04:53.751 --> 00:04:56.462
Why get a bunch of them together
to do this?

00:04:56.546 --> 00:04:59.215
We picked out the ones
that were higher in rankings.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.218
House pets are not typically able
to donate 100,000 yen,

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.679
but if it's 10,000 yen,
that's much more doable.

00:05:04.762 --> 00:05:07.181
10,000 yen from 100 people?

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:09.267
Well, that adds up to a million yen.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.184
So you--

00:05:10.268 --> 00:05:14.647
We can weed out the strongest contenders,
have them play higher-stakes games,

00:05:14.731 --> 00:05:17.942
collect the winnings,
and buy everyone out of being a house pet.

00:05:18.526 --> 00:05:20.862
This is how we can destroy the system

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:23.406
before we take on
the Student Council President.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.243
Enough talk. I wanna play a game.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.954
-There's a certain one you'll like.
-Huh?

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:33.541
This particular one
requires multiple people to participate.

00:05:33.624 --> 00:05:36.336
That's why I asked
a couple of your friends to tag along.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.049
If you end up winning,
you walk away with a million yen.

00:05:41.132 --> 00:05:43.092
Consider it a gift from me to you.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.224
[Mary gasping]

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.435
Please, Mary.

00:05:52.935 --> 00:05:54.228
Please help me save them.

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:07.241
Hello, all you sad singles!

00:06:07.825 --> 00:06:10.995
Were your lonely tears
all that kept you company last night?

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.126
Great! Thank you all very much.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.253
I'm happy to say you can stop crying!

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.674
<i>Welcome to the 50th Annual Coupling Party!</i>

00:06:23.758 --> 00:06:26.969
<i>There have been</i>
<i>over 5,000 participants thus far!</i>

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.013
<i>Many of our happy alumni</i>
<i>have stayed together</i>

00:06:29.097 --> 00:06:31.015
<i>and gotten married after graduating!</i>

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:33.226
I wonder what kind of drama we can expect

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:35.770
from the couples coming up
for our 50th year.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.940
<i>Best of luck trying to find the one</i>
<i>out there tonight, everybody!</i>

00:06:39.023 --> 00:06:40.775
What the hell is going on?

00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:43.945
How is this gonna destroy
the Student Council?

00:06:44.028 --> 00:06:46.030
Is this guy messing with me?

00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:49.325
<i>It's the Coupling Game!</i>

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:53.079
<i>Ladies will confess their love</i>
<i>to a special someone!</i>

00:06:53.162 --> 00:06:55.790
<i>Gentlemen will choose</i>
<i>their special someone!</i>

00:06:55.873 --> 00:06:59.085
I should add, getting coupled up is only
for the purposes of the game.

00:06:59.168 --> 00:07:01.129
So, please have fun and don't be creepy!

00:07:01.212 --> 00:07:02.922
Just relax and enjoy the ride.

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:06.384
<i>But as long as your heart is open,</i>
<i>there have been countless times</i>

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:08.928
<i>that something here</i>
<i>has grown into something more.</i>

00:07:09.011 --> 00:07:11.556
<i>It's okay to have some expectations.</i>

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:14.058
All right. Listen up. Sort yourselves out.

00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:16.561
<i>We need girls and boys on teams of five.</i>

00:07:16.644 --> 00:07:18.855
<i>Once you find your team, we'll move on to…</i>

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.148
<i>Step one.</i>

00:07:20.231 --> 00:07:21.482
<i>Conversation time!</i>

00:07:21.566 --> 00:07:24.819
<i>Deepen your friendship</i>
<i>and try to find your special someone.</i>

00:07:24.902 --> 00:07:25.736
<i>Next is…</i>

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:26.821
<i>Step two.</i>

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:28.364
<i>Consultation! </i>

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:31.159
<i>Talk to your team</i>
<i>and decide who you wanna pick.</i>

00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:32.368
<i>Finally…</i>

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.536
<i>Step three.</i>

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.121
<i>Confession time! </i>

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:37.707
<i>One of the ladies</i>
<i>will select someone on the men's team</i>

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.709
<i>to confess their love to.</i>

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.962
<i>The men will choose</i>
<i>whose confession they will accept.</i>

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:45.423
<i>Once everyone filled out their cards,</i>

00:07:45.506 --> 00:07:48.342
<i>the ladies will announce</i>
<i>who they confess their love for.</i>

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:49.594
<i>We'll do this in order.</i>

00:07:49.677 --> 00:07:52.138
<i>For those who are lucky enough</i>
<i>to become a couple,</i>

00:07:52.221 --> 00:07:53.639
<i>the man is the winner! </i>

00:07:53.723 --> 00:07:56.434
<i>The lady pays the man</i>
<i>the amount they bet to play.</i>

00:07:56.517 --> 00:07:59.979
<i>The men who don't have a partner</i>
<i>at the end will lose.</i>

00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:02.482
<i>They will pay the amount</i>
<i>they bet to the ladies.</i>

00:08:02.565 --> 00:08:06.819
Now, in this game, men and women
will both be betting the same amount,

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:09.989
but women are a little shy
when money and dating are put together.

00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:11.407
<i>With that in mind,</i>

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:14.827
<i>we have a special incentive tonight</i>
<i>for the ladies.</i>

00:08:14.911 --> 00:08:17.538
<i>The Maiden's Promise!</i>

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.666
<i>If a lady declares</i>
<i>any of these prior to play,</i>

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.960
<i>they will take on that obligation</i>
<i>after they lose</i>

00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:26.005
<i>in exchange for</i>
<i>a large reduction of their wager.</i>

00:08:26.088 --> 00:08:27.590
For the fellas out there,

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:30.259
the risk involved may come
with some big rewards.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:34.347
You'll only have once chance to confess
your love and choose that person.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.766
Let's get excited to find love, everybody!

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:41.771
Does this high school seriously have
parties to hook up a bunch of stray kids?

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:43.731
I did not agree to this!

00:08:43.814 --> 00:08:46.651
There's no way I'm gonna be matched up
with some guy I don't even know!

00:08:47.235 --> 00:08:50.112
<i>But if we don't go along with this,</i>
<i>what would we do?</i>

00:08:50.613 --> 00:08:52.657
Hello, Mary Saotome.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.908
<i>-</i>Good to see you.
-Whoa!

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:57.078
Hey. You're… you're Mikura.

00:08:57.161 --> 00:08:58.120
You're here?

00:08:58.204 --> 00:08:59.539
Call me Sado, please.

00:08:59.622 --> 00:09:01.749
You don't deserve to use my first name.

00:09:01.832 --> 00:09:04.126
So what brings you to this?

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.129
-Finding a boyfriend?
-Of course, not. Disgusting!

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:10.633
-Huh?
-My only purpose here is business. Look.

00:09:11.175 --> 00:09:14.387
Mistress Juraku is the head manager
for this party.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.515
I'm here to assist her
in its flawless execution.

00:09:17.598 --> 00:09:19.016
<i>Great. She's here?</i>

00:09:20.518 --> 00:09:22.895
You think
we should have Mary Saotome participate

00:09:22.979 --> 00:09:24.355
in the coupling game?

00:09:24.438 --> 00:09:25.273
Yeah.

00:09:25.356 --> 00:09:27.567
That isn't what we discussed.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.778
I thought you were going
to incorporate her into your plans?

00:09:31.279 --> 00:09:34.115
I feel like you're trying
to sneak into my territory.

00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:38.035
And if you are, I'll eat you!

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:40.913
Understood.

00:09:45.001 --> 00:09:46.752
[all groaning]

00:09:46.836 --> 00:09:49.297
Back to business.
You came as a group of three?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.423
Oh. Yeah.

00:09:50.506 --> 00:09:53.259
Then I'll introduce you
to two more players.

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:55.511
You want the two of us
to hop on their team?

00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:56.429
Yes.

00:09:56.512 --> 00:09:58.055
What's up!

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.933
Second-year from Sakura class,
Kurumi Kurume.

00:10:01.017 --> 00:10:02.685
I'm excited to play!

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:06.147
Third-year from the Botan class,
Chitose Inui.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.690
It's so great to meet you guys!

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.568
Yeah. Nice to meet you.

00:10:10.651 --> 00:10:13.821
So have any of you lovely ladies
ever been able to participate

00:10:13.904 --> 00:10:15.531
in the coupling party before?

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.408
This is the first time I've ever done it.

00:10:17.491 --> 00:10:18.826
We've never played either.

00:10:18.909 --> 00:10:20.286
Oh, how fun!

00:10:20.369 --> 00:10:23.289
I'll try and break everything down
for you as best I can.

00:10:23.372 --> 00:10:26.751
I've been playing the last couple years,
so I know how these things tend to go.

00:10:26.834 --> 00:10:29.337
Sounds like you didn't find a boyfriend.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.339
Don't mention that.

00:10:31.422 --> 00:10:34.342
I got paired up one of the last times
the school did this,

00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:36.385
and they told me it was how the game
was supposed to be gambled.

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:38.596
And then when I asked him out,
he told me no.

00:10:39.221 --> 00:10:41.098
What was so wrong with me
that he said no?

00:10:41.182 --> 00:10:44.393
This is wrong.
None of this is fair!

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:47.104
Let's just try and focus
on doing our best.

00:10:47.938 --> 00:10:49.148
You're so right.

00:10:49.231 --> 00:10:51.317
Sorry. Kinda spaced out a minute.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.611
Well, first, we fill out our lineup card!

00:10:53.694 --> 00:10:55.321
Lineup card?

00:10:55.404 --> 00:10:57.990
We fill this out
and turn it in to the front.

00:10:58.074 --> 00:11:01.118
This is gonna determine the order
that we confess or make decisions.

00:11:01.202 --> 00:11:03.120
So I can write down all our names.

00:11:03.204 --> 00:11:06.374
-Oh. I feel like I should also ask…
-Huh?

00:11:06.457 --> 00:11:08.751
Do you want a boyfriend or money?

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:11.253
Which one of those
are you going to prioritize today?

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:13.756
If we aren't open about what we want,

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:16.509
we might accidentally end up
working against each other.

00:11:16.592 --> 00:11:19.595
If you're here for a man, then the timing
on when you make your confession

00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:21.347
is gonna be <i>really</i> important.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.350
And the guys only have one chance
to say whoever they want to pick.

00:11:24.433 --> 00:11:26.519
But going early
doesn't always guarantee you'll win!

00:11:26.602 --> 00:11:28.521
I only came here for the money.

00:11:28.604 --> 00:11:30.523
I'm cool just going along with the group.

00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:36.404
Fine. All right then.

00:11:36.487 --> 00:11:39.949
Then we can just us Rock Paper Scissors
to figure it out, or whatever.

00:11:41.242 --> 00:11:43.244
[classical orchestral music playing]

00:11:43.744 --> 00:11:45.996
All set! Our lineup is in!

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.164
Thanks, Inui.

00:11:47.248 --> 00:11:50.209
I think
we're gonna get lucky today.

00:11:50.292 --> 00:11:52.169
They said we can go take our seats
over that way.

00:11:59.844 --> 00:12:02.221
[MC] <i>Has everyone taken their seats?</i>

00:12:03.013 --> 00:12:03.973
Awesome!

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:07.059
Then that means it's time
for you all to get to know each other.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.563
<i>Conversation time, begin!</i>

00:12:10.646 --> 00:12:12.815
I guess I'll start us off.

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:16.068
Nobuya Sera. I'm excited to play.

00:12:16.152 --> 00:12:19.071
Haruto Kibashira. Nice to meet you.

00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:20.698
I'm Ren Kochi.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:23.701
I'm Mamoru Kuonji.

00:12:24.285 --> 00:12:27.246
<i>All these guys seem</i>
<i>to be ridiculously good-looking.</i>

00:12:27.329 --> 00:12:29.457
<i>Why would any of them want to be here?</i>

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.334
I'm Kanade Musubi. Happy to be here!

00:12:33.127 --> 00:12:35.296
<i>Although,</i>
<i>I guess there's one exception.</i>

00:12:35.379 --> 00:12:36.589
Your turn, ladies.

00:12:36.672 --> 00:12:38.591
Okay.

00:12:38.674 --> 00:12:40.468
I'm Chitose Inui.

00:12:40.551 --> 00:12:43.679
I'm here to find a boyfriend
that can treat me like a princess.

00:12:43.763 --> 00:12:46.348
I'm excited
about maybe finding the one this time!

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:47.433
<i>That's good.</i>

00:12:47.516 --> 00:12:50.269
<i>It's better for us if they don't know</i>
<i>our goal is to make money.</i>

00:12:50.352 --> 00:12:52.605
<i>She's doing a great job fooling them.</i>

00:12:52.688 --> 00:12:55.900
And all of you are gorgeous,
so this is gonna be fun!

00:12:55.983 --> 00:12:58.486
<i>She is fooling them, right?</i>

00:13:00.571 --> 00:13:04.492
Wow. So the three of you
really run a gambling den?

00:13:04.575 --> 00:13:06.494
Doing something like that's
a lot of hard work.

00:13:06.577 --> 00:13:09.997
Well, yeah.
It would be if we were open right now.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.082
So what kinda guy are you into?

00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:14.001
I'm sure you like dudes
that are really smart.

00:13:14.084 --> 00:13:15.920
Oh. No, not really.

00:13:16.003 --> 00:13:18.172
Lucky. So what is your type then?

00:13:18.255 --> 00:13:19.465
Hmm.

00:13:20.049 --> 00:13:22.718
Someone who is so honest
that they're stupid,

00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:24.178
If I'm picking one.

00:13:24.261 --> 00:13:26.305
<i>Why did I answer that honestly?</i>

00:13:26.889 --> 00:13:28.098
Hey, Hanatemari.

00:13:28.182 --> 00:13:30.935
You've been sitting real quiet
ever since we started.

00:13:31.018 --> 00:13:33.145
Don't hold back because you're a pet.

00:13:33.229 --> 00:13:34.563
Tell me about your hobbies.

00:13:34.647 --> 00:13:37.024
Well, I guess I like to cook.

00:13:37.107 --> 00:13:39.610
And needlework I'll do sometimes.

00:13:39.693 --> 00:13:40.945
But I also like to--

00:13:41.028 --> 00:13:42.988
Cooking and needlework?

00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:46.450
Incredible!
You're a prime example of femininity!

00:13:48.702 --> 00:13:50.788
[Kanade] You're exactly my type.

00:13:50.871 --> 00:13:52.456
This is amazing!

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.292
All right, lovers! Time is up!

00:13:55.376 --> 00:13:57.586
Did you find anybody out there
that you might like?

00:13:58.254 --> 00:14:00.965
<i>Let's move on to consultation!</i>

00:14:04.051 --> 00:14:05.511
How does the betting work?

00:14:05.594 --> 00:14:07.972
I don't remember her explaining that
during the rules.

00:14:08.055 --> 00:14:10.516
Hmm?
It was on the registration form.

00:14:10.599 --> 00:14:12.977
Oh. We had a direct invite.

00:14:13.561 --> 00:14:15.104
It's one million yen per round.

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:18.649
[Mary] <i>That's too expensive! </i>

00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:21.318
<i>Dammit! I see what game he's playing now.</i>

00:14:21.402 --> 00:14:23.654
<i>He's testing me to see</i>
<i>if I can handle this.</i>

00:14:23.737 --> 00:14:25.865
<i>If I'm not experienced enough</i>
<i>to get through this,</i>

00:14:25.948 --> 00:14:27.616
<i>he'll just toss me to the side.</i>

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.995
That means we'll probably need
to offer the "dinner date" benefit.

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:35.875
-Why don't we try using the "sleep over"?
-[both] Huh?

00:14:35.958 --> 00:14:38.043
All of us would end up saving some money.

00:14:38.127 --> 00:14:40.129
We could try and have them
in the same room.

00:14:40.212 --> 00:14:41.255
Doesn't that sound fun?

00:14:42.131 --> 00:14:43.757
Do you not know what that means?

00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:45.926
Uh, Hanatemari,

00:14:46.468 --> 00:14:49.013
a "sleep over" is when you go
to a guy's house and they--

00:14:51.015 --> 00:14:53.392
[Mary] <i>Did she seriously have no idea?</i>

00:14:53.893 --> 00:14:55.227
Now that we've shot that down,

00:14:55.311 --> 00:14:58.272
we can go ahead and offer the dinner date
to lower our wagers.

00:14:58.856 --> 00:15:00.733
As for the specifics of our plan,

00:15:00.816 --> 00:15:03.736
we'll prevent as many couples
as possible to win.

00:15:03.819 --> 00:15:05.654
Otherwise, we'll end up owing.

00:15:05.738 --> 00:15:08.657
To ensure this, everyone should confess
to someone different.

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:11.076
If all of us confess to the same guy,

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.412
it increases our chances of coupling up.

00:15:13.996 --> 00:15:16.916
Tsuzura should definitely not
be confessing to Musubi.

00:15:16.999 --> 00:15:19.293
Yeah.
He seemed to take quite a liking to her.

00:15:19.376 --> 00:15:22.838
Oh! Could I pick Kuonji to confess to?

00:15:22.922 --> 00:15:24.173
Hmm? Why?

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:27.509
Did you see
how hot his glasses made him look?

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:31.180
Sure, he might not have talked a lot,
but I love the quiet types.

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:34.934
-I might even offer the "sleep over"…
-And I'll fill this out for everyone else.

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:37.937
Just make these picks, all right?

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.647
Any objections?

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.190
No objections.

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:42.942
Great. Let's go!

00:15:43.025 --> 00:15:45.861
Consultation time is almost over.

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:48.364
Please start making your way back
to your seats.

00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:52.159
-Tsuzura.
-Huh?

00:15:52.242 --> 00:15:55.788
Don't let any of the others know,
but let's switch our confessions up.

00:15:55.871 --> 00:15:57.539
Huh? Why, Mary?

00:15:57.623 --> 00:15:59.291
I'm just being extra careful.

00:15:59.375 --> 00:16:01.377
There's a pretty big flaw in this plan.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.670
It's a countermeasure.

00:16:02.753 --> 00:16:04.838
If there's one traitor among us,

00:16:04.922 --> 00:16:06.924
there's a danger that we'll all lose.

00:16:08.092 --> 00:16:11.470
[Mary] If someone tips off the guys
about who is confessing to whom,

00:16:11.553 --> 00:16:12.680
we're all done for.

00:16:12.763 --> 00:16:14.306
I understand.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:15.975
But Togakushi…

00:16:16.058 --> 00:16:18.060
I'm sorry, but I don't trust her yet.

00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:19.937
-Really?
-Tsuzura.

00:16:20.729 --> 00:16:23.399
Now is not the time
for us to be hesitating.

00:16:23.482 --> 00:16:25.526
We need to walk away from this as winners.

00:16:25.609 --> 00:16:26.443
You hear me?

00:16:26.527 --> 00:16:28.195
Okay.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.198
CONFESSION TIME

00:16:31.281 --> 00:16:33.909
And now it's the moment
you've all been waiting for.

00:16:33.993 --> 00:16:35.452
It's confession time!

00:16:35.536 --> 00:16:37.204
<i>Yeah! Take the risk!</i>

00:16:37.287 --> 00:16:38.956
<i>Let's put those hearts out there!</i>

00:16:39.039 --> 00:16:41.542
I'll be attending the needs
of your table for tonight.

00:16:41.625 --> 00:16:42.459
I'm Sado.

00:16:42.543 --> 00:16:44.044
Thank you for joining us.

00:16:44.128 --> 00:16:45.462
<i>It's her again.</i>

00:16:45.546 --> 00:16:49.466
Ladies, please circle the number
of the person you would like to confess to

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.968
and pass it to me.

00:16:51.051 --> 00:16:53.887
Gentlemen, please take these five cards.

00:16:53.971 --> 00:16:56.390
The numbers are the same
as your lineup card.

00:16:56.473 --> 00:16:58.976
I will collect these
after each confession.

00:16:59.059 --> 00:17:01.228
Would anyone like to declare a benefit?

00:17:01.311 --> 00:17:03.731
Yeah. I'd like the "dinner date."

00:17:03.814 --> 00:17:06.233
-I'd like to do that too, please.
-Me too.

00:17:06.316 --> 00:17:08.402
Your choices are noted.

00:17:08.485 --> 00:17:10.237
Please begin your confessions.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.905
I get to start us off.

00:17:11.989 --> 00:17:14.283
Which of you is it gonna be?

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:16.076
<i>Seems like no problems yet.</i>

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.286
<i>If we played normally,</i>

00:17:17.369 --> 00:17:20.247
<i>we'd have to expect</i>
<i>at least one couple to form from this.</i>

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:24.251
<i>Even if we did have a traitor that told</i>
<i>the guys who we were gonna confess to,</i>

00:17:24.334 --> 00:17:26.211
<i>Tsuzura and I would still win.</i>

00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:28.922
Gentlemen, it's your turn.

00:17:29.006 --> 00:17:31.759
Please indicate on a card
the lady you would like to select.

00:17:31.842 --> 00:17:34.303
So, man, who you picking?

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:37.389
I don't think I'm into girls
that wear a lot of makeup, you know?

00:17:37.973 --> 00:17:40.809
<i> I feel like something's off,</i>
<i>but I don't know why.</i>

00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:42.644
Okay. My turn!

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:45.564
Hey, Kibashira, I like you.

00:17:45.647 --> 00:17:47.149
Wanna go on a date with me?

00:17:48.734 --> 00:17:50.903
I'm just kidding!

00:17:53.238 --> 00:17:55.282
Uh-oh. My joke flopped.

00:17:55.365 --> 00:17:58.285
<i>Wow. None of them picked her?</i>

00:17:58.368 --> 00:18:00.537
<i>Why didn't any of those guys react at all?</i>

00:18:02.122 --> 00:18:04.124
All right. Next person, please.

00:18:04.208 --> 00:18:05.042
Oh. Right.

00:18:06.752 --> 00:18:08.504
I pick Musubi.

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:10.506
Next lady, please.

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:12.007
Uh, okay.

00:18:14.843 --> 00:18:15.761
CIRCLE THE OBJECT…

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:17.638
I'm picking Sera.

00:18:17.721 --> 00:18:18.639
Huh?

00:18:18.722 --> 00:18:21.433
Not me? Why choose him?

00:18:21.517 --> 00:18:22.893
I thought we were getting along!

00:18:22.976 --> 00:18:25.771
That wasn't who we agreed
you would pick, Hanatemari.

00:18:25.854 --> 00:18:27.523
Yukimi.

00:18:27.606 --> 00:18:29.900
It's part of my strategy to win.

00:18:29.983 --> 00:18:32.820
Sorry I didn't get a chance to tell you.
Hang tight for a bit.

00:18:33.529 --> 00:18:35.823
If you say so.

00:18:35.906 --> 00:18:37.825
Let's move forward. Next player.

00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:39.201
Oh. Right.

00:18:44.623 --> 00:18:47.751
[MC] <i>All right!</i>
<i>You're doing a great job, everybody!</i>

00:18:47.835 --> 00:18:51.421
All of our players have finally finished
turning in their confession cards.

00:18:51.505 --> 00:18:54.424
All that's left now is the results!

00:18:56.093 --> 00:18:57.845
<i>I've done everything that I can.</i>

00:18:57.928 --> 00:19:00.264
<i>With this plan, we should be able to win.</i>

00:19:00.347 --> 00:19:02.307
I have your table's results.

00:19:02.391 --> 00:19:03.767
-The order will be--
-Yes!

00:19:03.851 --> 00:19:05.394
We go in confession order,

00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.187
but if it's okay, I want last.

00:19:07.271 --> 00:19:08.772
-My heart's…
-That'll be fine.

00:19:08.856 --> 00:19:09.773
Let's just get it done.

00:19:10.566 --> 00:19:11.942
That won't be a problem.

00:19:12.025 --> 00:19:14.278
The first confessor, Kurumi Kurume.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:17.156
Her confession was made to Kibashira.

00:19:17.239 --> 00:19:18.282
Our results,

00:19:18.907 --> 00:19:19.867
we have a couple.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.287
Oh, crap. I got it, right?

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.664
Hmm? Were you hoping
to have a chance at the money?

00:19:26.373 --> 00:19:29.543
That's cool. I'd still be down
for going on a real date with you.

00:19:29.626 --> 00:19:31.670
Please leave courting until later.

00:19:31.753 --> 00:19:34.673
Our next confession was from Togakushi,

00:19:34.756 --> 00:19:36.300
and was delivered to Musubi.

00:19:36.884 --> 00:19:38.302
Another successful couple.

00:19:38.385 --> 00:19:39.303
Huh?

00:19:40.804 --> 00:19:43.599
I also have strong opinions
about literature.

00:19:43.682 --> 00:19:45.184
We will get along great.

00:19:45.767 --> 00:19:48.270
You wagered a dinner date.
Have I got that right?

00:19:49.271 --> 00:19:52.691
I'll find us somewhere romantic
and make a reservation.

00:19:53.275 --> 00:19:55.027
<i>This can't be a coincidence.</i>

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.821
<i>What is the likelihood</i>
<i>we'd have two couples in a row?</i>

00:19:57.905 --> 00:20:00.699
<i>So that means</i>
<i>we really do have a traitor here.</i>

00:20:01.283 --> 00:20:04.578
<i>Kurumi and Yukimi aren't off the hook</i>
<i>because they got paired up.</i>

00:20:04.661 --> 00:20:06.496
<i>The traitor would try</i>
<i>to cover their tracks</i>

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.582
<i>by giving themselves a match too.</i>

00:20:08.665 --> 00:20:11.585
<i>I'm glad I planned</i>
<i>that countermeasure with Tsuzura.</i>

00:20:11.668 --> 00:20:13.587
Next up, Hanatemari.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:14.838
We have another couple.

00:20:14.922 --> 00:20:15.839
Huh?

00:20:15.923 --> 00:20:18.050
Followed by Saotome,

00:20:18.133 --> 00:20:19.343
who made another couple.

00:20:19.426 --> 00:20:21.345
-What?
-Last is Inui.

00:20:21.428 --> 00:20:23.180
Another happy couple.

00:20:23.263 --> 00:20:24.890
Congratulations.

00:20:24.973 --> 00:20:26.391
We have five couples.

00:20:26.475 --> 00:20:27.684
Such an accomplishment.

00:20:27.768 --> 00:20:29.186
Enjoy, ladies.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.438
I don't understand.

00:20:33.023 --> 00:20:34.691
So great! He agreed!

00:20:36.193 --> 00:20:38.570
Well, this didn't play out
like we thought it would.

00:20:38.654 --> 00:20:39.947
What the hell?

00:20:42.783 --> 00:20:44.117
This is bullshit!

00:20:44.201 --> 00:20:45.827
I refuse to accept this at all!

00:20:46.536 --> 00:20:47.621
Calm yourself.

00:20:47.704 --> 00:20:49.831
Is there something
you're trying to imply here?

00:20:49.915 --> 00:20:51.375
Of course, there is!

00:20:51.458 --> 00:20:53.794
How could there be five couples
at one table?

00:20:53.877 --> 00:20:57.089
Tsuzura and I swapped our choices
before we even made the confessions.

00:20:57.172 --> 00:21:00.842
We wanted to protect ourselves in case
someone shared our picks with the guys.

00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:02.678
It isn't possible
to have this many matches

00:21:02.761 --> 00:21:04.263
unless someone cheated!

00:21:04.346 --> 00:21:06.473
I will not tolerate accusations.

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:09.601
I caught you cheating just the other day--

00:21:09.685 --> 00:21:11.353
What's wrong, Mary?

00:21:11.436 --> 00:21:13.855
Is there a problem I can help you with?

00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:15.357
<i>Sachiko Juraku!</i>

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.359
<i>Is she the one behind this?</i>

00:21:18.193 --> 00:21:20.529
Yeah, there is!
I'm calling out your scheme--

00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:23.865
Stop. I won't stand here and listen
to any more of your accusations.

00:21:23.949 --> 00:21:26.827
No house staff has altered your results.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.496
I can guarantee you that
with the utmost confidence.

00:21:29.579 --> 00:21:31.748
Do you really expect me to believe that?

00:21:36.211 --> 00:21:37.379
Mary.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:40.757
Don't be blinded by your own failure.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.010
There's another way.

00:21:43.093 --> 00:21:47.639
A completely different,
much simpler possibility.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.726
<i>Was there something I missed?</i>

00:21:50.809 --> 00:21:53.312
<i>Even if we did end up</i>
<i>getting betrayed by someone,</i>

00:21:53.395 --> 00:21:55.897
<i>there was no way that everyone</i>
<i>would still become paired up.</i>

00:21:56.815 --> 00:22:00.402
<i>The only thing that makes sense</i>
<i>is that management cheated.</i>

00:22:04.197 --> 00:22:06.658
[Mary] <i>No. I refuse to believe that.</i>

00:22:07.326 --> 00:22:09.286
<i>There's no way that can be right.</i>

00:22:10.829 --> 00:22:13.665
<i>What if the traitor is Tsuzura?</i>

00:22:14.249 --> 00:22:17.252
<i>If management is telling the truth</i>
<i>and they didn't cheat,</i>

00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:19.171
<i>then it would make total sense.</i>

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.175
<i>Tsuzura was the only one that knew</i>
<i>our confessions were gonna be different.</i>

00:22:24.259 --> 00:22:27.804
<i>Why was Tsuzura having that meeting</i>
<i>with Mibuomi before I got there?</i>

00:22:28.597 --> 00:22:30.182
<i>What were they talking about?</i>

00:22:30.932 --> 00:22:33.477
<i>Maybe they're working together</i>
<i>to entrap me</i>

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:35.729
<i>for standing up</i>
<i>against the Student Council,</i>

00:22:35.812 --> 00:22:38.690
<i>and she worked out some sort</i>
<i>of sweetheart deal for herself?</i>

00:22:39.274 --> 00:22:41.943
<i>But wouldn't that mean Yukimi</i>
<i>was in on it too?</i>

00:22:44.029 --> 00:22:46.281
<i>Of course, Juraku would be in on it.</i>

00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:49.201
<i>I bet they're all working together</i>
<i>to bring me down!</i>

00:22:49.284 --> 00:22:52.412
Well done.
That will conclude the first round.

00:22:52.496 --> 00:22:54.956
Now it's time to get started
with the bonus game.

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:55.957
Begin round two!

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:58.710
<i>Buy-in will be doubled at two million yen.</i>

00:23:01.463 --> 00:23:03.715
Now, then. What are you going to do?

00:23:04.383 --> 00:23:07.761
Aoi gave you so much money,
and you just lost it all.

00:23:07.844 --> 00:23:10.972
You know you're going
to be a house pet at this rate, right?

00:23:11.056 --> 00:23:13.934
But I don't have
two million yen.

00:23:14.017 --> 00:23:16.353
You don't need that much.

00:23:16.436 --> 00:23:19.272
No worries, girl. Kurumi's got you.

00:23:19.356 --> 00:23:20.857
But I can only do 20,000 each.

00:23:20.941 --> 00:23:21.775
Huh?

00:23:21.858 --> 00:23:24.444
You'll have to add the "sleep over"
to your wager.

00:23:24.528 --> 00:23:26.405
This is going to be so much more fun.

00:23:27.197 --> 00:23:28.657
What a great idea.

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:30.409
Do you like that option?

00:23:30.492 --> 00:23:32.244
What do you say, Mary?

00:23:32.744 --> 00:23:34.162
Mary, no.

00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:38.875
<i>Shut up!</i>
<i>I don't want anyone else to talk to me.</i>

00:23:38.959 --> 00:23:39.876
<i>No more.</i>

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.879
<i>I'm so sick of being conned</i>
<i>by these people!</i>

00:23:46.049 --> 00:23:46.925
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:23:48.009 --> 00:23:49.428
<i>What </i>can<i> I do?</i>

00:23:51.805 --> 00:23:54.266
<i>I… I don't know who I can trust!</i>

00:25:24.606 --> 00:25:25.941
[music fades]
